Redis 7.2.16 test framework: give the next test a fresh connection after a
failed test. The suite runs the tests of a unit on one shared connection; a
failed test can leave it in RESP3, in raw mode or with unread replies, and
every later test of the unit then reads shifted replies and fails, so one
failure hides the verdicts of the rest. After a failure the shared connection
is replaced by a new one in the mode (RESP2 or RESP3, raw or not) the failed
test started in. No command, assertion or expected value changes, no test is
excluded, and a passing test touches nothing. Apply to Firn and Redis
reference runs alike; retire when the pinned suite restores the connection
itself.

Sources:
https://github.com/redis/redis/blob/7.2.16/tests/support/test.tcl
https://github.com/redis/redis/blob/7.2.16/tests/test_helper.tcl

